# SystemOneSDK 0.6.0

## Endpoint and provider selection
{: .col-2}

```bash
export TYPESAFE_API_KEY="provider-key"
export TYPESAFE_BASE_URL="https://your-typesafe-host.example/deployment"
export TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL="provider-model-id"
```

```elixir
client = SystemOneSDK.new_client(
  api_key: key,
  base_url: "https://your-typesafe-host.example/deployment",
  model: "provider-model-id"
)
```

The base URL is the root before `/v1/models` and `/v1/systemone`; path prefixes are
retained. Use the selected provider's key/model and TypeSafe operation contract. A
generic OpenAI-compatible endpoint is not automatically TypeSafe-compatible.

## Client and questions
{: .col-2}

### Strict semantic API

```elixir
client = SystemOneSDK.new_client()
questions = [
  urgent: SystemOneSDK.noul("Urgent?"),
  team: SystemOneSDK.choice("Team?", billing: "Payments", technical: "Product"),
  severity: SystemOneSDK.score("Severity?", ["Low", "High"])
]
prepared = SystemOneSDK.prepare!(questions)
{:ok, response} = SystemOneSDK.evaluate(client, state, prepared)
```

### Tuple constructors

```elixir
SystemOneSDK.Question.Noul.new("Urgent?", true: "Time-sensitive")
SystemOneSDK.Question.Choice.new("Team?", [billing: nil, technical: nil])
SystemOneSDK.Question.Score.new("Severity?", ["Low", "High"])
```

Each also has `new!`. Legacy `SystemOneSDK.Noul/Choice/Score.new` still returns
legacy structs; `system_one` still uses string response keys.

## Answers and policy
{: .col-2}

```elixir
team = SystemOneSDK.Response.fetch!(response, :team)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.Choice.ranked(team)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.Choice.margin(team)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.confidence(team)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.gate(team, act: 0.9, review: 0.7)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.yes?(response.answers.urgent, 0.85)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.Score.expected_level(response.answers.severity)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.Score.max_level(response.answers.severity)
SystemOneSDK.Answer.Score.normalized(response.answers.severity)
SystemOneSDK.Response.values(response)
# %{urgent: 0.91, team: :billing, severity: 1.7}
```

Thresholds are explicit application policy, not safety guarantees. Expected and
modal Score levels differ; Noul confidence is derived as max(p, 1-p).

## Batch, errors and tests
{: .col-2}

```elixir
SystemOneSDK.evaluate_many(client, states, prepared,
  max_concurrency: 8, max_pending: 32, ordered: true, on_error: :collect,
  task_timeout_ms: 40_000, attempt_timeout_ms: 5_000)
SystemOneSDK.evaluate_stream(client, states, prepared, ordered: false)
SystemOneSDK.Error.retryable?(error)
SystemOneSDK.Error.retry_after(error)

client = SystemOneSDK.Test.client()
client = SystemOneSDK.Test.stub(client, urgent: {:noul, 0.9})
# Run application code, then verify before the creating process exits.
SystemOneSDK.Test.verify!(client)
SystemOneSDK.Test.close(client)
```

Unordered results have batch_index; errors use details.batch_index. Request
`timeout` and retry policy values still use seconds. Retries can repeat processing.

## Contract and operations tools

```bash
mix typesafe.capabilities
mix typesafe.record --output tmp/live --base-url "$TYPESAFE_BASE_URL" --model "$TYPESAFE_DEFAULT_MODEL"
mix reach.check --arch --smells
```

Recording needs a real API key; no live data is fabricated. Unadvertised transport
bounds remain unverified. Semantic telemetry excludes automatic prompt/state data.


## 0.3 runtime controls
{: .col-2}

```elixir
cancel = Pristine.Cancellation.new()
{:ok, response} = SystemOneSDK.evaluate(client, state, prepared,
  cancellation: cancel,
  max_request_bytes: 262_144,
  response_contract: [on_unknown_answer: :error])

SystemOneSDK.Prepared.keys(prepared)
SystemOneSDK.Prepared.fingerprint(prepared)
SystemOneSDK.Response.metadata(response)
SystemOneSDK.RuntimeCapabilities.report(client)
```

Per-call retry keys inherit omitted client retry fields; `retry: false` disables
retry for that call. Cancellation uses Pristine directly and cannot prove that a
remote service did not begin processing a request.

## 0.4 OTP and answer telemetry
{: .col-2}

```elixir
# Successful evaluate/4 calls emit one event per known answer:
[:system_one_sdk, :answer]
# measurements: confidence, top_probability, distribution_margin
# metadata: answer_type, question_index, model/request ID, Prepared fingerprint

children = [
  {Task.Supervisor, name: MyApp.TypeSafeTasks},
  {MyApp.Triage,
   client: client,
   task_supervisor: MyApp.TypeSafeTasks,
   max_in_flight: 32}
]
```

`MyApp.Triage` uses `SystemOneSDK.OTP.Server` and returns `{:evaluate, ...}` from
callbacks. The SDK starts no global task supervisor. See `guides/otp-server.md`
and `guides/recursive-decisions.md`.
